# Front door - Caddy holds requests while app.py restarts.
#
# Why: app.py restart = kill + start (single-instance mutex, no overlap possible) = 5-9 s with nobody on :80,
#      every user on the dashboard got bounced. Staging measurement, 10 s restart:
#      direct 18 errors (GET and POST) -> through this file 0 errors (longest wait 9.8 s).
#
# Started by caddy_ctl.py (boot bat + watchdog), never by hand.
# Env from caddy_ctl: APP_PORT (app.py, loopback), FRONT_PORT (default 80), LOG_DIR.
#
# Traps found in the staging experiment (do not "simplify" these away):
#  - Site address must be host-agnostic (http://:80). With http://127.0.0.1:80 Caddy answers requests for
#    the public Host header with an EMPTY 200 - the whole site blank.
#  - header_up -X-Forwarded-For: the app treats any X-Forwarded-For as "from outside"; Caddy adds one by
#    default -> bots/watchdog internal routes would be refused. CF-Connecting-IP passes through untouched,
#    so the app's client-IP helper is unchanged.
#    App-side contract this relies on: "internal" = remote_addr is loopback AND no Cloudflare header
#    (CF-Connecting-IP, Cf-Ray, ...) AND no X-Forwarded-For - every public request arrives through
#    cloudflared, which always sets the CF headers. Internal-only routes additionally require a shared key
#    header, so "looks local" alone never opens them.
#  - bind loopback only: behind Caddy every request reaches app.py from 127.0.0.1. If LAN/VPN could hit
#    Caddy directly, a request with no Cloudflare headers would look "local". cloudflared runs on this PC.
#  - Requests being processed at the exact kill moment: GET is retried here (200), POST fails (502) -
#    same as before Caddy, and rare (requests take tens of ms).
#  - lb_try_duration 45s, not 20s: the production cutover held a request 19.7 s - the restart script
#    registers a task, then app.py boots. 20 s had no margin; past it users get 502.
#  - admin off = no live reload. Config changes apply by restarting Caddy (gap ~0.7 s; a Windows client
#    retries a refused loopback connect for ~2 s, so it is not seen).
{
	admin off
	auto_https off
	log {
		output file {$LOG_DIR}/caddy.log {
			roll_size 5MiB
			roll_keep 3
		}
		level WARN
	}
}

http://:{$FRONT_PORT:80} {
	bind 127.0.0.1 [::1]
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{$APP_PORT} {
		lb_try_duration 45s
		lb_try_interval 250ms
		header_up -X-Forwarded-For
	}
}
